# walk-cache.manifest — rows for the terrain walk-vs-cache check
# (scripts/check_terrain_walk_cache.sh); both row forms are described there.
#
#   pose row  <level> | pos=(x, y, z) yaw=Y pitch=P | [lod]
#   bk2 row   <bk2> | <VBL> | <canon|inter> | [lod]
#
# Each row is captured native-only at 16:9 twice, once through the CPU terrain
# walk and once through the retained GPU terrain cache
# (OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1); the differing pixel count per row is
# compared with tests/golden/spyro-2/walk-cache-baseline.tsv.
#
# Plain boot (no attract-demo.bk2: the title screen and attract demo), VBL 3400
# sub-tick present at alpha 0.5, --lod original: 1 px at (357,185) on one
# untextured LP face (sector 96 face 5, one level in blue); the canonical
# present at the same VBL reads 0.
attract-demo | 3400 | inter | original
